  "raw": ", combustion-free technology has achieved 1 million zero emissions driving miles on a 120 kWh battery. And guess who gets to record the first real-world drives. Sounds pretty great!\nUlrich Hackenberg, the chief tech officer of VW Group BlueFoundation (which VW and the EEBB have been developing separately), announced yesterday that his company is ready to begin scaling up production. Meaning: we might be seeing Volvo V60 Emissions cars in your driveway not long after its big reveal next year!\nUlric Hackenberg recently arrived in Brussels to announce certain key milestones….\nNext big milestone will come… is it 2018 already or what!? Think you can guess it! #VolvoPebblemeisterpic.twitter.com/W6iq1tJBlq — Tommy Geitner (@ABIEnglish) September 8, 2017\nWe’re glad to hear Mr. Hackenberg say this, although it does undercut one of Head of Public Relations for Volv",
